From: gogo <gogo@bluedynamics.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:20:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add --stdin to read piped log lines; fix SSH partial-line
 handling

- New Source::Stdin (source: stdin) reads stdin non-blockingly on the
  render timer, so any command can be piped in, logstalgia-style:
    ssh me@server docker logs --follow --tail 1 web | gl_tail --stdin
- bin/gl_tail: --stdin/-, --parser/-P NAME, --name/-N NAME. With
  --stdin the config file is optional (dist/config.yaml defaults) and
  its servers: section is replaced by the stdin source.
- Config.parse_yaml/YamlParser accept top-level overrides.
- SSH source: parse only complete lines and keep partial ones buffered
  (it parsed fragments and dropped the rest of split lines).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013kYwHzrj5ef427USqzf3UF
